<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Åsta Gudbrandsdatter</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Åsta Gudbrandsdóttir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Åsta Gudbrandsdatter was a Norwegian noblewoman of the late 10th and early 11th centuries, according to the sagas. She was the mother of King Olaf II Haraldsson by her first husband, Harald Grenske, and by her second husband, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigurd-syr">Sigurd Syr</a>, petty king of Ringerike, the mother of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-hardrada">Harald Hardrada</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asta-gudbrandsdatter.jpg" alt="Åsta Gudbrandsdatter" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Halfdan Egedius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olav_den_helliges_saga_-_Kong_Olav_med_sine_halvbroedre_-_H._Egedius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
